Not sure I really follow what you're asking here, but you almost certainly don't want that sigma_alpha line inside the loop.  Doing so multiplies that prior into the posterior J times!

Also, you should be able to vectorize the normal distributions if you are willing to sacrifice a little readibility for (potentially) a lot of speed.  See the block() command which extracts a submatrix and that entire double loop can collapse down into a single line.

Cheers,
Marcus

