I just checked and the Cauchy distribution should be vectorized so if you had:

parameters {
  ...
  real<lower=0> sigma_alpha[J];
  ...
}

Then:

model {
  ...
  sigma_alpha ~ cauchy(0,0.25);
  ...
}

should work just fine.  If it doesn't, what error does it produce?

> Thanks for the block suggestion. Any chance you could point me to an example?

For a single sigma_alpha:

block(alpha,1,2,J,T-1) ~ normal(block(alpha,1,1,J,T-1),sigma_alpha);

should work.

For different sigma_alphas you'll need to loop over J:

for (j in 1:J) {
  block(alpha,j,2,1,T-1) ~ normal(block(alpha,j,1,1,T-1),sigma_alpha);

}

